      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِقْضَابٌ</span></b>  One <i>whose craft,</i> or <i>occupation, is that
of cutting</i> [app. <i>herbage &amp;c.</i>]. (Ham p. 490.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِقْضَبٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <i>Land that produces</i>
(M, K) <i>abundantly</i> (K) <i>the herbage called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَضْب</span>
<i>which is eaten when freshly cut,</i> (M, * K, TA,)
i. e. [<i>the species of trefoil,</i> or <i>clover, called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِصْفِصَة</span>.
(TA.)

